      "problem": "Given that $\\dfrac {2a^2(1+b)} {3b}  =x$ and $\\dfrac {1+b}{5b^2} =y ,$ then what is $x \\div y?$",
      "worked_solution": "To compute $x \\div y,$ i.e., \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{a}^{2}(1+b)}{3b} & ÷\\frac{1+b}{5{b}^{2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {2a^2(1+b)} {3b}  \\div  \\dfrac{1+b}{5b^2}&=\\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac {2a^2(1+b)} {3b}  \\cdot  \\dfrac {5b^2} {1+b}&=\\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac {2a^2\\cancel{(1+b)}} {3\\cancel{b}}  \\cdot  \\dfrac {5b^{\\cancel{2}}} {\\cancel{1+b}}&=\\[5pt]\n\t\t\\dfrac {10a^2b} {3}  \n\t}\n$$",
